# MedSign Cloud -- local secrets
#
# Copy to .env, or just start the backend: it writes this file itself on first run.
# .env is gitignored. .env.example is not, which is the whole difference between
# them and the reason this file has no key in it.

# The JWT signing key: an EC P-256 private key, PKCS#8, base64, on one line.
#
# Put a prepared key here and MedSign Cloud uses it as-is; leave it empty and
# Signing/EnvFileSigningProvider generates one on first run. Every access token
# MedSign Cloud issues is signed with it, which means anyone who can read this line
# can mint a valid doctor token for any account on this instance -- without touching
# the backend, without a password, and without leaving a trace anywhere.
#
# There is no PIN on it, no rate limit, no audit log, and a copy of it works exactly
# as well as the original. Exercise 2 moves it into a YubiHSM, where none of those
# sentences stay true.
MEDSIGN_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=

# Your YubiHSM Authentication Key, for exercise 2: the key id as 4 lowercase hex
# digits followed by your password, e.g. 1001hunter2. Prefer setting MEDSIGN_HSM_PIN
# in the environment -- this backend does not read it from here.
# MEDSIGN_HSM_PIN=
